# Benchmark harness, dumps and downloaded datasets. Deliberately untracked:
# the dumps are regenerated every run, and the DABstep context files are
# someone else's data that the repo has no business redistributing.
#
# `benchmark/*` and not `benchmark/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the negation below is silently dead against the
# directory form.
benchmark/*

# Except the handover. It is the document that tells the next session where
# everything stands and which reruns mean what, and it was living on one
# laptop's disk with no history — the one file in that directory that is
# writing rather than data.
!benchmark/HANDOVER.md

# And except the harness itself, which is code and not a dump. Every test round
# had been growing its own send_X/dump_X pair on the VPS, unversioned, so a fix
# to one never reached the others and nothing accumulated between rounds. These
# were committed once already and silently ignored, which would have left the
# whole point of them — that the harness outlives the round — undone.
!benchmark/chaos.sh
!benchmark/await_reply.mjs
!benchmark/check_reply.mjs
!benchmark/task_subject.mjs
!benchmark/capture_fixture.mjs
!benchmark/send_task.mjs
!benchmark/tasks.mjs
!benchmark/send_wave.mjs
